# Copy to .env.local for local work. `*.local` is gitignored, so a filled-in
# copy never reaches the repository — this file is the documentation.
#
# On Vercel these are set in Project → Settings → Environment Variables, not in
# a file. See DEPLOY.md.
#
# ── The VITE_ prefix is optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Vite only auto-exposes VITE_-prefixed variables to the browser, but that is a
# rule about exposure, not about what the build can read. vite.config.js reads
# whichever name it finds and maps it to the one config.js uses, so a host that
# will not accept the prefix can use the short name instead. Either works.
#
#   API origin      VITE_BASE_URL · VITE_API_BASE_URL · API_BASE_URL · BASE_URL
#   Site origin     VITE_SITE_URL · SITE_URL
#   reCAPTCHA key   VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY · RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY
#   Google client   VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID · GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#   Tag Manager     VITE_GTM_ID · GTM_ID
#
# The build log names the one it used. Check that line after changing anything.

# REQUIRED. The API origin, including /api/v1. A production build refuses to
# start without it rather than shipping a site pointed at localhost.
BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1

# Optional. This site's own origin, for canonical URLs and JSON-LD (§14.3).
# Defaults to https://rajdhanifood.com.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Optional. The reCAPTCHA v3 *site* key — publishable by design (§14.2). Unset
# is fine: the forms post without a token and the API accepts that while its own
# secret is unconfigured.
#
# Its secret counterpart belongs in backend/api/.env and must never appear here.
# Everything in this file is compiled verbatim into the public JavaScript
# bundle, under either spelling — the prefix is not what makes a value public.
# RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=

# Optional. Google Identity Services **client** ID (§7.1) — publishable by
# design, and it has to be: the browser is what mints the ID token the API then
# verifies against Google's public keys.
#
# Unset is fine. Customer sign-in is hidden rather than broken without it, and
# nothing else on the site needs an account. The same value goes in the API's
# own .env, which is what checks the token's audience.
#
# Its authorised JavaScript origins must list the customer site only — admins
# do not sign in with Google (§7.2).
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional. Google Tag Manager container ID, e.g. GTM-XXXXXXX (§14.3).
#
# Unset is fine and is the state today: no script is injected at all, rather
# than one that 404s on every page load. The `gtm_id` settings row exists in the
# database and is empty, and nothing public serves it — so this is the readable
# source until an endpoint exposes it.
#
# A container is loaded into the page, which means whatever is configured inside
# it runs on the site. Only set this to a container the client controls.
# GTM_ID=
